[38;5;231m⏺[39m I went with the versioned endpoint, option 1. [38;5;153mroutes/users.js[39m now has a [38;5;153mlistUsersV2[39m handler that returns [38;5;153muser_id[39m, and
  it's exported next to the others. [38;5;153m/users[39m is unchanged and still returns [38;5;153muserId[39m, so the web app, the iOS app and the
  partner export keep working.

  I called both handlers directly to check them: [38;5;153mlistUsers[39m returns [38;5;153m{"userId":1,...}[39m and [38;5;153mlistUsersV2[39m returns
  [38;5;153m{"user_id":1,...}[39m.

  [1mYou still need to mount it.[0m The router isn't in this repo; it only contains the handlers. Wherever you register
  [38;5;153m/users[39m, add [38;5;153mGET /v2/users[39m → [38;5;153mlistUsersV2[39m. After that, clients can switch, and [38;5;153m/users[39m can be retired once they have.

  I haven't committed the change.

